public import CFSG.Quasithin.ChapterK.Section01To04.SporadicCatalogue.RudvalisExclusion

/-!
# Source reductions for the K.4 sporadic representation catalogue

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004, K.4, printed
p.457. The degree-window reductions retain the full ambient cubic hypothesis,
actual F*(G), arbitrary central covers and all ambient outer actions.

The Rudvalis source exclusion is proved in every finite dimension and applied
to the catalogue sieve. The catalogue still requires the bounded M11, J1 and J4 exclusions,
the HS and He exclusions, and the genuine marked module recognitions for M12,
simple/triple M22, M23, M24 and J2. In particular the J2 recognition must retain
its G2(4) embedding and outer field compatibility. These are independent source
obligations, not assertions established by this module. No ratio calculation
on an already recognized surviving module is needed for this reduction.
-/
